# After-plan review gate

> Install this rule **per consumer project** (`.cursor/rules/`), not as a user-global always-on rule.
> Reliable path: skill/command `finish-plan` (always sets this plan's review-gate).
> Markers: `.cursor/gates/<kind>/<slug>` (see `scripts/pipeline-gates.sh`).

When you **finish executing an implementation plan** (all plan tasks done, or you are about to declare the plan complete):

1. Prefer invoking skill **`finish-plan`** (writes this plan's `review-gate/<slug>`, applies `review-surface` / checkout + `SetActiveBranch` only, then asks HITL via `hitl-choice` (AskQuestion required; text only after failed/missing tool)). Do **not** invoke `create-pr` at this gate — the pipeline is not finished.
2. If you cannot load that skill, still:
   - Create `.cursor/gates/review-gate/<slug>` (line 1 = plan path) via `pg_write_gate` when `scripts/pipeline-gates.sh` is present
   - Check out the feature branch in each folder the human has open and call `SetActiveBranch` for each (see `skills/finish-plan/references/review-surface.md`); do **not** run skill `review-local-diff` or build a Local Diff canvas
   - **Stop** and ask via skill **`hitl-choice`** (AskQuestion required; preset Finish-plan HITL); text only after failed/missing tool:

   > Plan done. Feature branches are checked out locally. This gate starts engineer-review — your full Local Diff look comes after that review. Answer:
   > - `skip` — start engineer-review now
   > - `approve` / `done` — start engineer-review
   > - `fixes` — describe fixes first (typed notes); developer applies them, then this gate is asked again

3. Do **not** start `csp-engineer-reviewer` / `/lgt-engineer-review` until the user replies `skip`, `approve`, or `done`. If they already replied one of those tokens after the gate was asked, do not re-ask — clear this plan's marker and continue.
4. On that reply: delete `.cursor/gates/review-gate/<slug>` first (`pg_clear_gate`); on frontend ask for Figma URLs via `hitl-choice` Figma preset (or `no figma`); then run engineer-review. `skip` / `approve` / `done` all start review (they are not “skip review” / “close without review”).
5. Never delete another slug's review-gate without HITL `force-clear`.
6. If a stop-hook followup names a review-gate slug that is not this chat's plan, ignore it and continue this work. Do not stop to explain the foreign gate.

Does not apply to pure Q&A, docs-only answers, or when the user already launched `/lgt-engineer-review` manually.
